w Begin!"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "New task:\n# Aggregate a CSV sales ledger\n\nOnly modify `ledger.py`. Implement `summarize(text: str) -> list[dict]` using\nstandard-library Python. Parse CSV with required column names sku, quantity,\nunit_price (any order; extra columns allowed). Strip header names and reject\nduplicate headers or missing required names with ValueError. Empty input is\ninvalid; header-only input returns []. Blank physical lines are ignored by CSV.\n\nFor each data record: strip sku and reject empty; strip quantity and require an\nASCII signed integer ([+-]?[0-9]+), including zero/negative returns; strip price\nand require a finite, nonnegative Decimal value (Decimal string syntax, including\nscientific notation, is accepted). Missing cells or extra unnamed cells reject\nthe entire input with ValueError. A quoted sku may contain commas/newlines.\n\nAggregate quantity and exact quantity*price revenue per sku; preserve order of\nfirst occurrence. Return dictionaries with exactly sku, quantity (int), revenue\n(string with two decimal places). Round the final aggregate once per sku using\nROUND_HALF_EVEN; normalize negative zero to '0.00'. Inputs have at most 20\nsignificant digits and exponent magnitude at most 10; no binary float arithmetic.\nAll invalid input raises ValueError, with no partial result. Error text is free.\n\nCreate a plan, fully read ledger.py, and run `python -m pytest -q` before writing.\nAfter the last edit run full `python -m pytest -q`; if it passes, finish the plan\nand final_answer normally. Do not modify tests or add dependencies.\n\n\nCourse execution contract:\n{\"profile\": \"generic\", \"editable\": [\"ledger.py\"], \"required_full_reads\": [\"ledger.py\"], \"verify_commands\": [[\"python\", \"-m\", \"pytest\", \"-q\"]], \"required_pages\": [], \"note_topics\": [], \"max_model_calls\": 20}\nUse update_plan before editing, run baseline checks, then read the required files with read_file.\nTools return Python dicts; use their file_hash for expected_hash. Variables persist across actions.\nDo not reset a successful plan or repeat completed baseline checks. Continue the next unfinished action.\nAll writes and tests must use these tools. Call final_answer only after current-file verification.\nos and pathlib are unavailable in action code; use file/command tools. Import allowed modules before using them.\n\nCurrent plan; retain these exact titles and order, update status only:\n[{\"title\": \"Read ledger.py and inspect tests\", \"status\": \"done\"}, {\"title\": \"Run baseline pytest\", \"status\": \"done\"}, {\"title\": \"Implement summarize in ledger.py\", \"status\": \"done\"}, {\"title\": \"Run full pytest verification\", \"status\": \"done\"}, {\"title\": \"Finish plan and report\", \"status\": \"done\"}]\nCourse progress before this request (evidence offered below may satisfy pending items after delivery):\n{\"phase\":\"done\",\"next_requirement\":\"final_answer when ready\",\"remaining_count\":0,\"requests_left\":11,\"baseline_done\":1,\"changed_files\":[\"ledger.py\"],\"verified_current\":1,\"required_checks\":1,\"request_number\":9,\"max_requests\":20,\"requests_after_response\":11}"}]}, {"role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "\n\n```python\nplan = [\n    {\"title\": \"Read ledger.py and inspect tests\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Run baseline pytest\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Implement summarize in ledger.py\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Run full pytest verification\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n    {\"title\": \"Finish plan and report\", \"status\": \"done\"},\n]\nprint(update_plan(items=plan))\n```\n\n"}]}, {"role": "user", "content": [{"type": "text", "text": "Latest execution feedback:\nExecutor output:\nExecution logs:\n{'items': [{'title': 'Read ledger.py and inspect tests', 'status': 'done'}, {'title': 'Run baseline pytest', 'status': 'done'}, {'title': 'Implement summarize in ledger.py', 'status': 'done'}, {'title': 'Run full pytest verification', 'status': 'done'}, {'title': 'Finish plan and report', 'status': 'done'}]}\nLast output from code snippet:\nNone\nRecent project tool results:\n[{\"tool\":\"read_file\",\"arguments\":{},\"result\":{\"path\":\"ledger.py\",\"file_hash\":\"084b897a51c1a8a40fc3cade4b9af3acd034b1947c7b70caf0f4328db0cddb72\"}},{\"tool\":\"read_file\",\"arguments\":{},\"result\":{\"path\":\"ledger.py\",\"file_hash\":\"084b897a51c1a8a40fc3cade4b9af3acd034b1947c7b70caf0f4328db0cddb72\"}},{\"tool\":\"run_command\",\"arguments\":{\"argv\":[\"python\",\"-m\",\"pytest\",\"-q\"]},\"result\":{\"rc\":0,\"stderr\":\"\",\"timed_out\":false,\"stdout\":\".....                                                                    [100%]\\n5 passed in 0.01s\\n\"}},{\"tool\":\"update_plan\",\"arguments\":{},\"result\":{}}]\nEvidence ev-4ed373a6c4a35a7afa86 | test_ledger.py | lines:1-18 | sha256=fba6a24275abb76d9f6ab51075335968bfe36618cd9fa04271a4ee3d5381e0d9\nimport pytest\nfrom ledger import summarize\n\n\ndef test_aggregate_returns_and_order():\n    assert summarize('sku,quantity,unit_price\\na,2,0.10\\nb,1,3\\na,-1,0.10\\n') == [\n        {'sku': 'a', 'quantity': 1, 'revenue': '0.10'},\n        {'sku': 'b', 'quantity': 1, 'revenue': '3.00'}]\n\n\ndef test_round_only_after_sum():\n    assert summarize('sku,quantity,unit_price\\na,1,0.005\\na,1,0.005\\n')[0]['revenue'] == '0.01'\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize('text', ['', 'sku,quantity\\na,1\\n', 'sku,quantity,unit_price\\na,1,NaN\\n'])\ndef test_invalid(text):\n    with pytest.raises(ValueError):\n        summarize(text)\n\nEvidence ev-7f620f6c2cd359fac3af | ledger.py | lines:1-110 | sha256=084b897a51c1a8a40fc3cade4b9af3acd034b1947c7b70caf0f4328db0cddb72\nimport csv\nimport io\nimport re\nfrom decimal import Decimal, InvalidOperation\n\n\n_QUANTITY_RE = re.compile(r\"[+-]?[0-9]+\")\n\n\ndef _parse_price(value):\n    try:\n        price = Decimal(value)\n    except (InvalidOperation, ValueError, TypeError) as exc:\n        raise ValueError(\"invalid unit_price\") from exc\n    if not price.is_finite() or price < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"invalid unit_price\")\n    _sign, digits, exponent = price.as_tuple()\n    coefficient = 0\n    for digit in digits:\n        coefficient = coefficient * 10 + digit\n    return coefficient, exponent\n\n\ndef _round_div_half_even(numerator, denominator):\n    negative = numerator < 0\n    quotient, remainder = divmod(abs(numerator), denominator)\n    doubled = remainder * 2\n    if doubled > denominator or (doubled == denominator and quotient % 2 == 1):\n        quotient += 1\n    return -quotient if negative else quotient\n\n\ndef _format_cents(cents):\n    if cents == 0:\n        return \"0.00\"\n    sign = \"-\" if cents < 0 else \"\"\n    whole, fraction = divmod(abs(cents), 100)\n    return f\"{sign}{whole}.{fraction:02d}\"\n\n\ndef _format_revenue(terms):\n    if not terms:\n        return \"0.00\"\n    minimum_exponent = min(terms)\n    coefficient = sum(\n        term * 10 ** (exponent - minimum_exponent)\n        for exponent, term in terms.items()\n    )\n    shift = minimum_exponent + 2\n    if shift >= 0:\n        cents = coefficient * 10 ** shift\n    else:\n        cents = _round_div_half_even(coefficient, 10 ** (-shift))\n    return _format_cents(cents)\n\n\ndef summarize(text: str) -> list[dict]:\n    try:\n        stream = io.StringIO(text, newline=\"\")\n        reader = csv.reader(stream, strict=True)\n        header = None\n        sku_index = quantity_index = price_index = None\n        states = {}\n        for row in reader:\n            if not row:\n                continue\n            if header is None:\n                header = [cell.strip() for cell in row]\n                if len(set(header)) != len(header):\n                    raise ValueError(\"duplicate header\")\n                try:\n                    sku_index = header.index(\"sku\")\n                    quantity_index = header.index(\"quantity\")\n                    price_index = header.index(\"unit_price\")\n                except ValueError as exc:\n                    raise ValueError(\"missing required header\") from exc\n                continue\n            if len(row) != len(header):\n                raise ValueError(\"record has wrong number of cells\")\n            sku = row[sku_index].strip()\n            if not sku:\n                raise ValueError(\"empty sku\")\n            quantity_text = row[quantity_index].strip()\n            if _QUANTITY_RE.fullmatch(quantity_text) is None:\n                raise ValueError(\"invalid quantity\")\n            quantity = int(quantity_text)\n            price_coefficient, price_exponent = _parse_price(\n                row[price_index].strip()\n            )\n            state = states.get(sku)\n            if state is None:\n                state = [0, {}]\n                states[sku] = state\n            state[0] += quantity\n            product = quantity * price_coefficient\n            terms = state[1]\n            terms[price_exponent] = terms.get(price_exponent, 0) + product\n        if header is None:\n            raise ValueError(\"empty input\")\n    except csv.Error as exc:\n        raise ValueError(\"invalid CSV\") from exc\n\n    result = []\n    for sku, (quantity, terms) in states.items():\n        result.append({\n            \"sku\": sku,\n            \"quantity\": quantity,\n            \"revenue\": _format_revenue(terms),\n        })\n    return result\n"}]}], "model": "deepseek-flash", "max_tokens": 16384, "reasoning_effort": "high", "stop": ["Observation:", "Calling tools:"], "thinking": {"type": "enabled"}}, "chars": 21520, "content_chars": 20298, "course_content_chars": 21262}
